From f11f43887b735f78c66271fb20bcd18c93baa8f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: anyingiit <49945850+anyingiit@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 19:14:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] docs: enable JAVADOC_BANNER so banner-style comments are
 rendered

Several files document themselves with Javadoc "banner" comments
(`/*****...`), e.g. search/binary_search.cpp, search/interpolation_search.cpp,
sorting/selection_sort_iterative.cpp, dynamic_programming/partition_problem.cpp
and geometry/graham_scan_*. With JAVADOC_BANNER = NO Doxygen treats these
as plain comments, so the @file blocks are ignored and the files show up
in bold without a page in the generated file list.

Set JAVADOC_BANNER = YES so these blocks are parsed as documentation.

Closes #3234
---
 doc/Doxyfile | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/doc/Doxyfile b/doc/Doxyfile
index 14101f4..53b227a 100644
--- a/doc/Doxyfile
+++ b/doc/Doxyfile
@@ -225,7 +225,7 @@ JAVADOC_AUTOBRIEF      = NO
 # interpreted by Doxygen.
 # The default value is: NO.
 
-JAVADOC_BANNER         = NO
+JAVADOC_BANNER         = YES
 
 # If the QT_AUTOBRIEF tag is set to YES then Doxygen will interpret the first
 # line (until the first dot) of a Qt-style comment as the brief description. If
-- 
2.43.0

